From b1b136639451ab45d157ed35521406062a8d1585 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:25:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(delegate): resume rebuilds a finished subagent from its
 stored session

delegate_task action='resume' refused any child without a finished-run
record: one spawned before records existed, one run under worktree
isolation, one cut off by a restart or whose end state was never
written. Every child's conversation is stored as its own session, so a
missing record is no reason to give up.

When the record or its end state is missing, resume rebuilds them from
the session: the messages, the goal and context stamped on it (or the
first user message), its model and endpoint, its place in the spawn
tree (a grandchild resumes under the child that spawned it), its
iteration cap and the worktree it ran in (checked out again from its
kept branch when removed). The parent's message is its next turn. The
record path is unchanged. A child that is still running is pointed to
steer; a session that is gone or holds no conversation is reported.
